You should run Pex/C# code through a debugger to observe the values and generate the assertions for your tests. But be aware that not all assertions are generated, especially if your test code doesn't branch or doesn't cover all possible outcomes, or if the code being analyzed is non-deterministic for its input.

The above is an example for one of the assertions. You can generate assertions for the rest of the code as per your needs.--------------------
